        "end_line": 27
      },
      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The code example at line 27 demonstrates saving rendered PDF pages to disk using `img.save('page_1.png', 'PNG')` without any user confirmation, warning, or path validation. In a skill context where users might invoke this automatically, an adversary could manipulate input parameters to write files to arbitrary locations, potentially overwriting sensitive system files or application code. The skill description claims broad capabilities including 'creating new PDFs' which compounds the risk if the underlying implementation lacks path sanitization.",
      "remediation": "Add explicit user confirmation before any file write operations. Implement strict path validation using `pathlib.Path.resolve()` to ensure writes remain within an intended directory. Sanitize all filename inputs to prevent directory traversal attacks. Document security considerations in the skill metadata and require users to specify output directories explicitly.",
      "code_snippet": null,
      "intent": null,
      "tags": []
    },
    {
